Z||000000||1986 Fiero||03-16-2001||10:56 AM||||I just bought a 1986 fiero with the 2.5 4cyl engine.It runs great and only has 74,000 miles on it but when i put it in drive (Automatic Transmition) it makes a clunking noise and shifts really hard making the car jerk.Am i just in need of a fluid and filter change or do i  have a bigger problem.<BR>             Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||03-16-2001||11:08 AM||||the motor mounts are probly failing... as for your other post.. uummm DON"T buy a chip! an MSD and a decent coil.. or if it's DIS.. just the MSD box and new plugs and wires. the easy K&N filer and a bigger exhaust and Cat. 2.25" would be just fine.. <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A>  they have Catco cats in the right size and a KILLER price. and <A HREF="http://www.spintechmufflers.com" TARGET=_blank>www.spintechmufflers.com</A>  for a decent muffler or <A HREF="http://www.powertone.com" TARGET=_blank>www.powertone.com</A>  that should help a bit.. if you can find a header that would free up even more... <P><BR>oh yeah.. welcome to the board! <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||varnster||03-16-2001||11:13 AM||||I had a problem a while ago similar with my<BR>auto 87 gt. My problem was the t.v cable or<BR>the detent cable leading from the throttle body to the tranny, it was in a bind and would not let the car shift correctly, it would rev high and i had to let off the gas and get back on it to shift, ive never had<BR>a 4 cyl but this could be something to check.<BR>kind of grabing at straws, but 9 out of 10<BR>times its something small and overlooked.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mr.Frosty||03-16-2001||02:30 PM||||I had that problem on a previous Formula<BR>I owned.It was a combination of motor mounts,<BR>transmission mount,and dogbone bushings needing to be replaced.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top <BR>85 GT Turbo||||reg||8
